\b Latest Version Feature List\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.15\par
- Summary: Extended the ESP32-C3 bridge into a SoftAP plus TCP server transport endpoint and aligned the firmware/documentation versions.\par
\par
\b X=0, Y=1\b0\par
\b 2026-03-12 14:34:13\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.15\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.15\par
- Summary: Promoted the ESP32-C3 bridge from USB-only framing into the simulator SoftAP/TCP transport endpoint.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` now brings up a visible `EyalSimulatorAP` SoftAP, owns a single-client TCP listener on `192.168.4.1:3333`, accepts framed transport traffic over both USB Serial/JTAG and TCP, and sends `client_connected` on TCP connect so the ESP32-S3 client can advance into keepalive. The bridge payload ceiling was increased to 256 bytes, stale TCP sessions are actively replaced or closed on reset, disconnect, and parse failure, and the transport design sources plus detailed design document were updated so the documented server-side flow matches the new firmware behavior.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - BRIDGE-20260312-1: The ESP32-C3 bridge exposed only USB framing, so the ESP32-S3 client could not reach the simulator transport path over Wi-Fi/TCP.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 17:20:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.13\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.12\par
- Summary: Refined the server-state display and release versioning policy for simulator-only revisions.\par
- Notes: Added a read-only `Text Received From Client` box under Server States, corrected the live-integer presentation so the server-side value appears on the server side and the client-side value appears on the client side, updated tests for received client payload visibility, and kept the firmware version fixed at `0.1.12` because this release changes simulator code only.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - UI-20260311-6: The server/client live-integer display and received-client visibility were ambiguous during operator review.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 17:05:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.12\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.12\par
- Summary: Refined the simulator operator UI and backend gating around connect completion, payload sending, and editable transport configuration.\par
- Notes: Corrected the connect-state logic so a generic bridge `connect_ack` no longer counts as real client connection success, added explicit initialize/connect pass gating for Keepalive and Send Data invokes, introduced a send-data payload text box populated with random encyclopedia-style sentences on each send, made transport profile edits overwrite the live config while preserving the field currently being edited during snapshot refresh, improved runtime error visibility in the flash banner, and added side-by-side connection-integer display under Server States.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - FLOW-20260311-3: The server runtime could advance past connect on bridge acknowledgement alone even when the real client had not connected.\par
  - UI-20260311-5: Snapshot refresh overwrote focused transport profile inputs, preventing operators from editing SSID, IP, and related fields.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 16:40:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.11\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.11\par
- Summary: Converted the server transport runtime from operator-stepped progression into an automatic reset-to-keepalive sequencer.\par
- Notes: Reset now clears buffered traffic, sends RESET, and arms automatic initialize progression; the runtime advances one stage at a time through initialize and connect during snapshot polling so the UI can observe the transition path; connect success automatically promotes the runtime to keepalive and enables send-data; command transmit failures now latch explicit stage-specific error text instead of surfacing only as raw request failures; the transport contract and detailed design were updated to describe the automatic server-state sequencing.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - FLOW-20260311-2: After reset, the simulator remained in reset until the operator manually invoked initialize instead of progressing automatically toward keepalive.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 16:20:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.10\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.10\par
- Summary: Reworked the server-state transport flow, extracted the shared ServerInterface layer, and aligned the operator UI with the implemented low-level behavior.\par
- Notes: Added the `ServerInterface` shared framing module and portable native protocol headers for later MCU reuse, converted the simulator runtime from the old disconnect-based flow to reset, initialize, connect, keepalive, send-data, and error states, made initialize auto-issue connect and wait for the ESP response, restricted error recovery to reset only, added the Send Data API route and UI button, renamed Machine State to Server States, updated the architecture baselines and regenerated the detailed design document, and kept serial reset behavior clearing buffered transport data before the next session.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - FLOW-20260311-1: The simulator still exposed a disconnect-centered transport state model that no longer matched the intended ESP controller workflow.\par
  - IFACE-20260311-1: Protocol framing rules were embedded only under the server transport package instead of living in a reusable shared interface boundary for later MCU integration.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 14:46:59\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.9\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.9\par
- Summary: Restructured the operator screens and versioned the navigation-alignment revision.\par
- Notes: Increased UI typography, split the operator surface into Screen 1 for Operational Control and Transport Profile, Screen 2 for Lifecycle Actions plus Machine State and Logger, and Screen 3 for Important Data, replaced the middle top-navigation action with a Lifecycle target, tightened and lightened the transport profile list styling, removed title-frame boxes, and corrected nav scrolling so each button compensates for the static dashboard header and per-screen header bar heights.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - UI-20260311-4: Navigation to screen groups landed below the intended top alignment and required repeated presses to reach the correct viewport position.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 14:13:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.8\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.8\par
- Summary: Refreshed the simulator operator dashboard and versioned the verified UI revision.\par
- Notes: Retitled the browser experience as Eyal Espresso Server Simulator, introduced a fuller dashboard shell with hero and summary cards, reorganized transport controls into grouped sections, improved runtime logger/status presentation, and added live summary chip updates for transport state, logger state, backend health, and build metadata.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - UI-20260311-3: The simulator UI looked like an unfinished transport template and did not present the runtime state in a clear operator-facing dashboard.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 13:56:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.7\par
- Summary: Simplified the simulator launcher window flow and versioned the startup-behavior fix.\par
- Notes: Removed the extra launcher console from the standard-user batch flow, changed the temporary PowerShell handoff to close automatically after startup, kept installation verification and browser prompting in the launcher phase, and updated the README plus detailed design so the documented launch contract matches the actual single-temporary-shell behavior.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - LAUNCH-20260311-1: The standard-user simulator launcher left an unnecessary PowerShell prompt window open after backend startup completed.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 11:59:47\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.6\par
- Summary: Standardized simulator script documentation and comment rules.\par
- Notes: Added file-level documentation blocks to every maintained PowerShell helper, filled in missing helper-function headers in the detailed-design generator, added intent-focused inline comments for non-obvious host-specific behavior, and updated README workflow rules to require strong script documentation plus comment and inline-code best practices.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - DOC-20260311-2: Simulator helper scripts did not use one consistent best-practice documentation standard, which made maintenance and review harder.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 11:51:01\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.5\par
- Summary: Formalized the simulator backend launch design and versioned the documentation update.\par
- Notes: Added a backend launch contract to the machine-readable transport design, updated the requirements and detailed design documents to describe the preferred repo-local launcher, `.venv` resolution, stdout/stderr visibility, `/health` readiness verification, stable host supervision, and cache-busted browser launch flow, and captured the rationale that backend correctness must remain separate from transient tool or sandbox process lifetime.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - DOC-20260311-1: Simulator backend launch guidance was incomplete and did not explicitly define the best-practice launch contract for Python plus `uvicorn` on this Windows host.\par
\par
